# Task 2 Report — PIT Optimizer Audit-Only USD Authorization

## Status

Complete. The schema-v3 authorization ledger now treats calls and tokens as the
only capacity authority. Pricing projections and authoritative provider cost are
durable audit evidence and never participate in capacity comparison.

No tests were added, modified, or run, following the binding production-first
ruling. No provider, Docker daemon, hidden data, upload, push, or subagent was
used.

## Commit

- Commit: `e65ab35e883568485c2318fa8d7ad1f8a572beb5`
- Subject: `Make PIT optimizer USD accounting audit-only`
- Committed production file: `core/pit_optimizer_authorization.py`
- Commit diff: 504 insertions, 188 deletions

## Exact API and record changes

### Advisory pricing

- Replaced `FrozenModelPricing` with `OptimizerPricingSnapshot`.
- The active fields are exactly `model`, `lookup_status`,
  `prompt_per_million`, `completion_per_million`, and
  `pricing_payload_sha256`.
- `lookup_status` accepts only `available` or `unavailable`.
- Available snapshots require finite, non-negative `Decimal` rates.
- Unavailable snapshots require both rates to be `None`.
- The pricing digest covers model, status, and canonical decimal-rate strings.
- `available(...)`, `unavailable(...)`, and
  `projected_call_usd(prompt_bytes, output_tokens)` are implemented.
- Pricing records serialize rates as canonical decimal text or JSON null.

### Active authorization dataclasses

- `OperatorAuthorizationGrant` now contains exactly `grant_id`,
  `additional_calls`, `additional_tokens`, and
  `policy_source_scope_sha256`.
- `OperatorAuthorizationWindow` now contains exactly `window_id`, `grant_ids`,
  `authorization_requirement_sha256`, `max_calls`, `max_tokens`, and
  `policy_source_scope_sha256`.
- `AuthorizationRunLease` now contains exactly `lease_id`,
  `one_shot_key_sha256`, `window_id`, `run_manifest_sha256`,
  `pricing_snapshot_sha256`, `pricing_status`, `projected_plan_usd`,
  `max_calls`, and `max_tokens`.
- `AuthorizationCallReservation` now contains exactly `reservation_id`,
  `lease_id`, `call_index`, `iteration`, `role`, `reserved_tokens`, and
  `projected_call_usd`.
- `PitOptimizerProviderFacts` now contains exactly `call_index`, `iteration`,
  `role`, `requested_model`, `returned_model`, `pricing_snapshot_sha256`,
  `outcome`, `request_started`, `response_received`, `finish_reason`,
  `response_schema_valid`, `accounting_complete`, `prompt_tokens`,
  `completion_tokens`, `total_tokens`, `cost_usd`,
  `retained_reservation_tokens`, and `audit_sha256`.
- Advisory plan/call projections are stored as canonical non-negative decimal
  text or null. Their magnitude is never compared with capacity.

### Schema-v3 ledger

- Active records use `schema_version=3` and exact closed key sets.
- `open_run_lease` validates manifest, requirement, scope, one-shot identity,
  pricing identity/status, and only call/token capacity.
- `open_run_lease` atomically appends adjacent `pricing_snapshot` and
  `lease_open` records.
- `reserve_call` enforces ordered sealed-plan identity and only call/token
  capacity. It accepts the keyword-only advisory `projected_call_usd`.
- Grants, windows, leases, and reservations contain no `max_usd`,
  `additional_usd`, `reserved_usd`, retained USD, nullable ceiling, infinity,
  or sentinel.
- Ledger replay revalidates manifest/scope identity, exact grant/window/lease
  capacity, pricing-to-lease binding, one-shot keys, reservation order, provider
  pricing identity, record indices, canonical JSON, record digests, and the hash
  chain.
- Pricing snapshots must be immediately and uniquely bound to a lease.
- The `record-grant` CLI no longer accepts `--additional-usd`.

### Reconciliation and terminal accounting

- Request not started records `charged_calls=0`, `charged_tokens=0`,
  `actual_cost_usd=0.0`, and `cost_accounting_status=not_started`.
- Complete accounting records one charged call, authoritative actual tokens,
  authoritative actual cost, and `cost_accounting_status=authoritative`.
- Started but incomplete accounting records one charged call, the full retained
  token reservation, null actual cost, and
  `cost_accounting_status=unavailable`; the lease closes terminally.
- Reconciliation overage now consists only of a token reservation overflow or
  cumulative calls/tokens beyond the lease.
- A resource overage is appended durably before raising and must have a
  `budget_exhausted` lease close.
- High finite authoritative cost is preserved in the reconciliation and gateway
  terminal commitment without producing capacity exhaustion.
- Gateway terminal commitments and charged-total recovery use the same
  calls/tokens plus explicit actual-cost audit state. Retained USD and USD
  charge-basis fields were removed.

### Immutable schema-v2 history

- Added `read_legacy_authorization_history(path)`.
- It verifies regular non-link input, complete newline-delimited records,
  duplicate-free canonical JSON, schema version, record indices, record hashes,
  and the previous-record hash chain.
- It returns a tuple of recursively immutable mappings/tuples.
- It never translates, rewrites, resumes, or appends schema-v2 records.
- Opening an active `AuthorizationLedger` on canonical schema-v2 history raises
  a clear `schema-v2 ... not resumable` error.

